---
description: Code comments and documentation standards
globs: "**/*.go"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Comments

All comments, godoc comments, Swagger annotations, TODOs, logs, and developer notes MUST be written in English.

Prefer expressive code over excessive comments.

Comments should explain:
- intent
- constraints
- architectural decisions
- non-obvious behavior

Do NOT comment:
- obvious code
- trivial operations
- self-explanatory logic

Avoid comments like:

// increment counter
i++

// call service
svc.Create()

---

# Godoc

Exported symbols should have concise godoc comments when behavior is not immediately obvious.

Godoc must:
- start with the symbol name
- describe intent
- avoid implementation details

Good:

// CreateOrder validates and persists a new order.

Bad:

// CreateOrder calls the repository to insert an order.

---

# TODOs

TODOs must:
- be actionable
- provide context
- describe the future improvement clearly

Good:

// TODO: Replace polling with Kafka consumer after rollout.

Bad:

// TODO fix this

---

# Avoid

- Spanish comments
- bilingual comments
- commented-out code
- debug notes
- implementation-history comments
- noisy comments
- redundant comments

Use logs for runtime observability instead of explanatory comments.